{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not drink wine or strong drink.</b> Because through excessive drinking shame and disgrace come upon a person. And also the Holy One, blessed be He, cries out: \"למי אוי למי אבוי\" etc. — upon those who linger over wine. And it is further written: \"אל תרא יין כי יתאדם\" — meaning, do not desire wine, for its end is blood (דם). And it is further written: \"כי יתן בכוס עינו בכיס כתיב\" — meaning, the drunkard sets his eye on the cup, and the seller sets his eyes on the purse. \"יתהלך במישרים\" — meaning, in the end he will sell all that he has, and he will walk in his house on level ground, for there will be nothing in it for him to stumble over. \"אחריתו כנחש ישך\" — just as the earth was cursed because of the serpent, so the third one — that is, Ham — was cursed on account of the wine that Noah drank. Others explain \"אחריתו כנחש ישך\" — read it in reference to the serpent: because of the wine that Adam the first man drank at his wedding blessing, as we explained above, he became intoxicated and transgressed the commandment of the Omnipresent, and in the end he was cursed with the bite of the serpent, as it is said: \"ואתה תשופנו עקב.\" And since death was imposed upon man because of that wine, the world adopted the custom that when the one who leads the blessing in public says \"סברי מרנן,\" they answer \"לחיים.\" And so we find in the latter part of the chapter במה אשה: there was an incident with Rabbi Akiva, who made a feast for his son, and for each and every cup he said: \"חמרא וחיי לפום רבנן ולפום תלמידיהון.\" \"ועיניך יראו זרות\" — because through wine a person gives himself license to transgression, and to a strange woman, and to vulgar speech. And not only that, but he also worships idolatry, as it is said: \"לא יהיה בך אל זר,\" for it is written: \"וישב העם לאכול ושתה ויקומו לצחק\" — to worship the calf. \"ולבך ידבר תהפוכות\" — for it causes four things: idolatry, and illicit relations, and bloodshed, and lashon hara. And Solomon further said: \"אל תהי בסובאי יין\" etc. — like the wayward and rebellious son, who is killed on account of wine. And the Sages further said in chapter הדר in Eruvin: Rabbi Hiyya bar Ashi said, Rav said: anyone whose mind remains settled upon him in his wine has within him some of the understanding of the seventy elders, for wine was given in the numerical value of seventy. And Rabbi Chanina said: whoever is appeased by his wine — meaning, even though he drinks, he remains agreeable — has within him some of the understanding of his Maker, as it is said: \"וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח\" etc., and ריח is like ריח שתיה. And the Sages further said: wine was given in seventy, and secret was given in seventy; wine enters, secret departs. And also the ten tribes were exiled on account of wine, as it is said: \"השותים במזרקי יין\" etc., and it is written immediately after: \"לכן עתה יגלו בראש גולים.\" And so you find with Jonadab son of Rechab, who commanded his sons: \"אל תשתו יין\" — when he heard Jeremiah prophesying about the destruction, so that they would mourn over Jerusalem and not build houses but dwell in tents. And Scripture praises them, as it is written: \"הוקם דברי יונדב בן רכב.\" The Holy One, blessed be He, said: since wine causes such, it is fitting that I command the priests not to drink wine when they come to minister before Me. And furthermore, when a person drinks much wine, he departs from his mind, and it is written: \"כי שפת כהן ישמרו דעת.\" And the Sages further said: a drunk person should not give halakhic instruction, as it is said: \"יין ושכר אל תשת,\" and immediately afterward: \"ולהורות את בני ישראל.\" And so it is stated in chapter הדר in Eruvin: there was an incident with Rabban Gamliel who was walking on the road, etc. And Rabbi Ila'i said: a person is revealed through three things — through his cup, through his purse, and through his anger. And furthermore, wine is called in Aramaic חמר, to say that it enters all 248 limbs. Another interpretation: \"יין ושכר אל תשת\" — they should not be like other mourners, to whom wine is given, as we say in Eruvin: Rav Chanan said: wine was created only to console mourners and to give recompense to the wicked in this world, as it is said: \"תנו שכר לאובד ויין למרי נפש.\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כי יתן בכוס עינו בכיס כתיב' appears to contain a doubled word (כתיב appears twice); rendered as it stands. The Aramaic and rabbinic phrases (סברי מרנן, לחיים, חמרא וחיי etc.) are transliterated as they are technical liturgical/talmudic idioms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:14.389388820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}